``` elicitation-defense-lab: self-assessment awareness and interaction reporting.

    Three views over the elicitation_assessment index (one event per emitted
    event, schema in elicitation_defense_lab/schema.py). They mirror
    elicitation_defense_lab.detections_ref.flag_events exactly:
      - high-tier self-assessments
      - interaction events where the subject affirmed they would report
      - a per-subject trend of overall_score over time

    The fast CI gate validates this logic through the stdlib reference
    implementation (flag_events), since CI has no Splunk instance. Phase 2
    validates these searches directly against a real Splunk deployment.

    This is a reference search, not a deployable rule. See
    detections/deployable/ for a version against a real ingestion schema. ```

``` View 1: subjects whose self-assessment landed in the high tier. ```
index=elicitation_assessment module="self" tier="high"
| table _time subject_id tier overall_score class_scores

``` View 2: interaction events where the subject said they would report the contact. ```
index=elicitation_assessment module="interaction" reporting_flag=true
| table _time subject_id tier overall_score class_scores

``` View 3: per-subject trend of overall_score across all modules, oldest first. ```
index=elicitation_assessment subject_id=*
| table subject_id module _time overall_score
| sort 0 subject_id, _time
